WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.642 --> 00:00:12.767
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:13.575 --> 00:00:15.785
Hey, something just occurred to me.

00:00:15.785 --> 00:00:19.237
Why do microbiologists
need a missile silo?

00:00:19.237 --> 00:00:23.418
That would be like our department
having a... medical bay.

00:00:23.418 --> 00:00:26.167
Mm, my gun feels light; I should reload.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:32.006
I suppose it's possible I won't encounter
anyone else hostile tonight, but...

00:00:32.006 --> 00:00:33.767
no, that's not possible.

00:00:35.056 --> 00:00:38.410
Yeah, it even has the red glow
of Hell lighting there.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:41.964
There must be a way out of here
that doesn't go straight through Hell.

00:00:41.964 --> 00:00:44.100
Well, if there's one thing I've
learned today,

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.468
it's that missile launches are
not like the movies at all.

00:00:47.468 --> 00:00:49.362
I thought there were all these procedures,

00:00:49.362 --> 00:00:51.389
two different people with special keys,

00:00:51.389 --> 00:00:54.034
a small crew of people to
monitor all the systems,

00:00:54.034 --> 00:00:57.019
but no. It's just a big red
button that says "Launch".

00:00:57.019 --> 00:00:57.459
[gunshot]

00:00:57.459 --> 00:00:58.596
DAAAH!

00:00:58.596 --> 00:01:00.614
WHERE THE FUCK DID THAT COME FROM?!

00:01:00.614 --> 00:01:01.033
[gunshot]

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:01.705
YEEE!

00:01:01.705 --> 00:01:03.949
I GOT IT THE FIRST TIME!

00:01:03.949 --> 00:01:05.692
I didn't see anyone.

00:01:05.692 --> 00:01:08.244
I may have seen a muzzle flash...

00:01:08.244 --> 00:01:09.700
I don't know...

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:10.601
Blehblblbluh...

00:01:11.115 --> 00:01:11.975
Okay...

00:01:11.975 --> 00:01:12.534
Blehblehbleh...?

00:01:13.477 --> 00:01:16.622
Maybe I've been too hasty to judge
about that underground passage.

00:01:16.622 --> 00:01:18.591
It's starting to look better now.

00:01:19.187 --> 00:01:20.819
Okay, go go go go go!

00:01:22.837 --> 00:01:23.467
Mehnuhn?

00:01:24.957 --> 00:01:25.500
Mehnununbid...?

00:01:26.821 --> 00:01:29.033
Then we're all in agreement,
let's take the ladder.

00:01:31.028 --> 00:01:36.133
Yeah, better to reign in Hell
than... get shot on the surface.

00:01:36.873 --> 00:01:39.843
Christ, those rounds left a
pockmark on this suit.

00:01:39.843 --> 00:01:41.853
I'm going to have welt marks for sure.

00:01:41.853 --> 00:01:43.956
Ah, another tram.

00:01:43.956 --> 00:01:47.236
I'm going to be depressed if all
this does is loop back to the old track.

00:01:48.013 --> 00:01:49.367
The hell is this?

00:01:50.481 --> 00:01:52.918
It looks like some sort of camera...?

00:01:53.402 --> 00:01:55.031
Can I sell this?

00:01:55.031 --> 00:01:58.107
It looks like good quality,
whatever it is.

00:01:58.107 --> 00:01:59.376
Does this come out?

00:01:59.376 --> 00:02:00.414
No.

00:02:00.414 --> 00:02:02.434
Oh, wait, there's some sort of
trigger on the back.

00:02:03.177 --> 00:02:04.932
[powering up]

00:02:04.932 --> 00:02:05.845
[chirps]

00:02:05.845 --> 00:02:07.434
Oh. Oh!

00:02:08.207 --> 00:02:10.033
I saw these.

00:02:11.151 --> 00:02:13.985
Okay, I think I'm done messing
with this one.

00:02:13.985 --> 00:02:16.300
I don't want to touch it anymore.

00:02:16.876 --> 00:02:17.961
I'll take this one.

00:02:17.961 --> 00:02:20.446
I just hope it doesn't turn on
while I'm carrying it.

00:02:20.446 --> 00:02:23.934
What the hell... it's like I'm
caught fishing line... there we go.

00:02:24.982 --> 00:02:27.234
All right, um... on.

00:02:29.075 --> 00:02:31.771
Hm, I just thought of a paradox.

00:02:31.771 --> 00:02:37.097
Maybe the more people I kill,
the less likely I am to be the fall guy.

00:02:37.097 --> 00:02:40.286
Because, sure, they could say I
killed five or ten people,

00:02:40.286 --> 00:02:46.226
but can they really pin dozens and
dozens of armed military personnel on me?

00:02:46.226 --> 00:02:49.088
[tram squealing]
I think--WHAT?  NO! NO NO NO!

00:02:49.088 --> 00:02:50.873
NOT AGAIN! I'M OUT!

00:02:50.873 --> 00:02:53.133
Ah ah! Uniform! Unif--

00:02:56.354 --> 00:02:58.099
New Yorkers talk like
they're all big and bad,

00:02:58.099 --> 00:03:00.667
I bet they don't deal with half
of this shit in the subway.

00:03:02.823 --> 00:03:05.762
I think if I ever hear someone
complain about their commute again,

00:03:05.762 --> 00:03:07.234
I'm just going to punch them in the face.

00:03:07.879 --> 00:03:10.868
"My drive home's worse than yours."

00:03:12.527 --> 00:03:14.653
Well, that's two more to add to the count.

00:03:14.653 --> 00:03:18.551
Yeah, I think it's going to hard sell
pinning all these killings on just me.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:20.681
What's this?

00:03:22.931 --> 00:03:25.161
This is useless. This doesn't go anywhere.

00:03:25.161 --> 00:03:25.676
What?

00:03:26.664 --> 00:03:29.018
Anyway, my background
doesn't fit the profile:

00:03:29.018 --> 00:03:30.442
no military training,

00:03:30.442 --> 00:03:31.933
never fired a gun,

00:03:31.933 --> 00:03:33.475
acquitted for petty theft,

00:03:33.475 --> 00:03:36.271
not a member of any
extremist organizations,

00:03:36.271 --> 00:03:38.690
has PhD in a theoretical physics.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.667
Yeah, that sounds like our man.

00:03:41.068 --> 00:03:43.319
What the hell is this room?

00:03:43.319 --> 00:03:45.393
I guess this is an
abandoned missile silo,

00:03:45.393 --> 00:03:48.652
since we got enough funding to
just keep making more of them.

00:03:48.652 --> 00:03:51.613
Of course, no ladder, no stairs.

00:03:51.613 --> 00:03:53.222
Guess I'll just drop down.

00:03:53.222 --> 00:03:55.434
So, who are some other spree killers?

00:03:55.913 --> 00:03:57.648
There's Timothy McVeigh.

00:03:57.648 --> 00:03:59.467
He had military training.

00:04:00.152 --> 00:04:02.783
Well, Lee Harvey Oswald
wasn't a spree killer,

00:04:02.783 --> 00:04:07.470
but he received about as much government
attention as I'm getting right now.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.567
He had military training...
and was an extremist.

00:04:11.543 --> 00:04:13.452
Ugh, that's gross.

00:04:13.452 --> 00:04:15.667
Hey! Get a room, you two!

00:04:18.932 --> 00:04:21.500
This is a FAMILY missile silo.

00:04:22.672 --> 00:04:24.534
I have nothing more to say to you.

00:04:25.123 --> 00:04:26.139
Who else?

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:28.533
Charles Whitman, military training.

00:04:28.533 --> 00:04:30.199
I'm a hard sell.

00:04:30.199 --> 00:04:30.601
I think--

00:04:34.705 --> 00:04:37.397
Christ, you people were
under the stairway.

00:04:37.397 --> 00:04:39.033
This place is low class.

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:41.073
Let's see.

00:04:41.073 --> 00:04:44.934
Alvin York killed dozens of
people and he was a hero.

00:04:44.934 --> 00:04:47.000
He didn't even want to; he was like me.

00:04:48.724 --> 00:04:49.922
Am I a hero?

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:50.921
Eh, I don't know.

00:04:50.921 --> 00:04:54.223
I don't think it's heroic if the only
person you're saving is yourself.

00:04:54.223 --> 00:04:55.780
I'll take that.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.020
Dammit, this whole place is flooded.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:00.519
Well, I'm running out of options here.

00:05:00.519 --> 00:05:02.435
All roads lead to water.

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:05.067
It would help if I had a clue
where I was going.

00:05:05.962 --> 00:05:08.182
I can't see a damned thing.

00:05:08.182 --> 00:05:10.701
Eh, screw it, maybe I'll find
somebody's car keys.

00:05:12.433 --> 00:05:21.227
[underwater mumbling]

00:05:21.227 --> 00:05:34.804
[underwater panicking]

00:05:34.804 --> 00:05:39.146
[gasping]

00:05:39.146 --> 00:05:39.979
WHAT GIVES?!

00:05:39.979 --> 00:05:42.391
SOMETHING WAS BITING ME DOWN THERE!

00:05:42.391 --> 00:05:44.508
This pool sucks, I'm getting out!

00:05:44.508 --> 00:05:46.156
At least, I think I am.

00:05:46.156 --> 00:05:48.719
I'm having that sinister feeling again

00:05:48.719 --> 00:05:54.534
where every hallway here looks it loops
back in on itself for no damned reason.

00:05:55.787 --> 00:05:57.309
Steady...

00:05:57.309 --> 00:05:57.838
Shit!

00:05:57.838 --> 00:06:04.667
[underwater mumbling]

00:06:05.981 --> 00:06:08.968
Yeah, the water is always
wetter on the other side.

00:06:09.857 --> 00:06:10.367
What the--

00:06:10.968 --> 00:06:12.029
What the hell is that?

00:06:12.029 --> 00:06:14.155
It looks like a prison guard tower.

00:06:14.155 --> 00:06:14.868
I don't get it.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:19.139
This place makes no sense.

00:06:19.139 --> 00:06:23.934
[underwater mumbling]

00:06:24.561 --> 00:06:25.986
...it's unconstitutional...

00:06:26.202 --> 00:06:33.834
[underwater mumbling]

00:06:34.537 --> 00:06:37.373
Okay, that passage is the
only one left, I think.

00:06:37.373 --> 00:06:38.580
I'll check out.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.533
If it I looks good, I'll keep going.

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:43.854
If it doesn't, I'll come back...
or die, I guess.

00:06:44.391 --> 00:06:44.787
No.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:55.267
[underwater panicking]

00:06:59.229 --> 00:07:05.313
[underwater straining]

00:07:05.313 --> 00:07:06.551
[gagging]

00:07:06.551 --> 00:07:11.891
[gasping]

00:07:11.891 --> 00:07:13.455
Oh dear God...

00:07:13.455 --> 00:07:14.781
Oh God...

00:07:14.781 --> 00:07:15.734
Oh jeez...

00:07:16.226 --> 00:07:18.502
Oh... oh...

00:07:18.502 --> 00:07:22.832
Okay, I think I'll take a breather.

00:07:22.832 --> 00:07:26.067
Oh man. That sucked.

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:32.436
And those worms or
whatever keep BITING ME!

00:07:32.436 --> 00:07:34.067
BLAGH!

